[0m[38;2;153;153;153m[48;2;55;55;55m❯ [0m[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;55;55;55mWithout using any tools, write a numbered list of 40 short fruit facts, one line each, then one closing sentence.[0m[48;2;55;55;55m                    [0m

[0m[38;2;255;255;255m● [0m1. Botanically, bananas count as berries but strawberries don't.
  2. A strawberry carries about 200 seeds on its outside.
  3. Apples float because about a quarter of their volume is air.
  4. Botanically, tomatoes are fruits.
  5. Avocados only start to ripen once they're picked.
  6. A pineapple plant takes about two years to produce one fruit.
  7. Fresh cranberries bounce and float because they have air pockets inside.
  8. A raspberry is made of many tiny fruits called drupelets.
  9. Kiwifruit used to be called the "Chinese gooseberry."
  10. Lemons are a hybrid of citron and bitter orange.
  11. Durian is banned on Singapore's public transit because of its smell.
  12. A grape cut in half and microwaved can produce a flash of plasma.
  13. A fig is really a cluster of flowers turned inward.
  14. Peaches, apples, pears and cherries all belong to the rose family.
  15. A coconut is a drupe, not a true nut.
  16. Watermelon is about 92% water.
  17. One pomegranate can hold several hundred seeds.
  18. The blue in blueberries comes from pigments called anthocyanins.
  19. The mango is India's national fruit.
  20. Each cashew nut grows below a fleshy fruit called the cashew apple.
  21. In English, the fruit was called "orange" before the color was.
  22. Bananas are slightly radioactive because they contain potassium-40.
  23. Panama disease nearly wiped out the Gros Michel banana, so the Cavendish replaced it.
  24. Apple seeds contain amygdalin, which can release cyanide when chewed.
  25. Dragon fruit grows on a cactus.
  26. Jackfruit is the largest fruit that grows on trees and can weigh over 40 kg.
  27. Miracle fruit makes sour foods taste sweet for a while after you eat it.
  28. Pears ripen best after they're picked.
  29. Olives are fruits, technically drupes.
  30. Plantains are starchy bananas that are usually eaten cooked.
  31. Unripe astringent persimmons make your mouth pucker because of their tannins.
  32. Grapefruit can interfere with how the body processes many medications.
  33. Papaya contains papain, an enzyme used to tenderize meat.
  34. Pineapple's bromelain breaks down protein, which is why it can make your mouth tingle.
  35. British sailors were nicknamed "limeys" because they ate citrus to prevent scurvy.
  36. China grows more apples than any other country.
  37. There are more than 7,500 known apple varieties.
  38. Clementines are a cross between a mandarin and a sweet orange.
  39. Kumquats are eaten whole, and the peel is the sweet part.
  40. A 1947 US customs ruling classified rhubarb, a vegetable, as a fruit.

  Whether botanical or legal, the word "fruit" turns out to mean much more than anything sweet in a fruit bowl.

